   "text": "I read the structure region by region and wrote the SMILES below. I have not run it through a parser, so validity is checked by hand only.\n\n**What the drawing shows**\n- **Macrocycle:** it is rapamycin-like but modified. The triene is replaced by a C(CH3)=CH\u2013CH(chain) unit, and the pyran carries a ring OMe and a ring CH3.\n- **Linker:** a three-CH2 chain ending in an amide to a piperazine. That piperazine is acylated with C(=O)CH2CH2NH\u2013, which attaches to the quinazoline.\n- **Quinazoline:** it has an 8-F, a 6-Cl, a 7-(2-fluoro-6-hydroxyphenyl) group and a 4-(4-acryloylpiperazinyl) group.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I assigned each stereocentre from the drawn wedges and hashes, using the neighbour order in the SMILES. The two C=C geometries come from the drawn positions of their substituents:\n- The ester-side C(CH3)=CH\u2013cyclohexyl alkene has the ester carbon trans to the ring.\n- The ring-internal C(CH3)=CH alkene has the chain trans to the CH2.\n\nSMILES: C[C@@H]1C[C@H](OC)[C@@H]%11O[C@@]1(O)C(=O)C(=O)N2CCCC[C@H]2C(=O)O[C@H](/C(C)=C/[C@H]6C[C@@H](OC)[C@H](O)CC6)[C@H](C)[C@@H](O)CC(=O)[C@H](CCCC(=O)N7CCN(CC7)C(=O)CCNc8nc(N9CCN(CC9)C(=O)C=C)c%12cc(Cl)c(-c%13c(O)cccc%13F)c(F)c%12n8)/C=C(C)/C[C@H](C)C[C@H](OC)%11"
